fxhoudinikimodo is covered by two different sets of terms, because it is a fork of
chordee/kimodo-houdini-bridge and still contains that project's code.

Read section 2 before assuming this repository is open source. It is not, taken as a
whole: the files listed there carry the upstream project's non-open-source terms, and
only their original author can change that.


