    docs/setup.md
    kimodo_server.py
    scripts/_add_help.py
    scripts/_soma77.py
    scripts/build_skin.py                 (unchanged from upstream)
    scripts/check_env.py
    scripts/create_hda.py
    houdini/otls/                         (generated by create_hda.py and build_skin.py)

Source: https://github.com/chordee/kimodo-houdini-bridge

That project ships no license file. Its README states, in full:

    This project (bridge code, HDA, scripts) is released for personal and research
    use with no restrictions.

    The NVIDIA Kimodo model is subject to its own license - see the Kimodo repository
    for terms before use.

Those are the only terms granted for this material, and they are reproduced here
rather than reinterpreted. A grant limited to "personal and research use" is not an
open source license under the Open Source Definition, whatever the trailing "with no
restrictions" was meant to convey. If you need broader rights, ask the upstream author
rather than relying on this file.

Valentin Beaumont's additions to the files above are substantial in several cases, and
are offered under the MIT terms of section 1 to the extent they can be separated from
the upstream work. That does not extend to the upstream work itself, which is why these
files are listed here rather than in section 1.


